Evidence packet written to `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Freddie-Mercury/2026-08-28_020004/evidence-packet.md` (`packet_status: complete`, SHA verified against `context.json`).

What the compilation found, briefly:

- **All transcript-anchored material held up.** Every Wigg 1985 and Freestone 2021/2025 quote the draft leans on was re-verified against the three on-file transcripts; the Dolezal 1987 "pretence" lines verified near-verbatim via Louder; Roger Taylor's disclosure quote pinned to Rolling Stone 2014; the corpus stat (80 musicians, 30 Fours) confirmed against `corpus-stats.json`.
- **Largest unresolved evidence gap (CLM-07):** the FAQ's claim that Mary Austin **"was holding his hand when he died."** No checked source supports it — accounts put Dave Clark "reportedly at the bedside," Hutton present per his memoir, Freestone in the house, and several say Mary was *the first phoned after* his death. It appears to have ridden in from an unsourced "Mary Austin at bedside" line in the creator-stage research file's timeline. Recorded as a disputed claim in a SERP-surfaced FAQ answer.
